Stellis Health downloads or calls the following third-party components. They are not
part of this repository and keep their own licences.

Speech models, downloaded on first start
- Whisper "small.en" in ggml format, from whisper.cpp (MIT).
  https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
- Pyannote segmentation 3.0, ONNX export distributed by sherpa-onnx (MIT).
  https://huggingface.co/pyannote/segmentation-3.0
- NVIDIA NeMo TitaNet small speaker model, ONNX export distributed by
  sherpa-onnx. Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0). https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

OCR tools, installed in the hosted image
- Tesseract OCR and English language data (Apache License 2.0).
  https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract
  https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast
- Leptonica image processing library (BSD 2-Clause).
  https://github.com/DanBloomberg/leptonica
  The image retains package copyright files in /usr/share/doc.

Native tools, installed by uv as Python packages
- FFmpeg, from the imageio-ffmpeg package (BSD 2-Clause wrapper). The FFmpeg
  executable it carries is built with GPL components and is licensed under the
  GNU General Public License version 3 (https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html).
  Stellis runs FFmpeg as a separate program and does not link it.
- whisper.cpp, through the pywhispercpp package (MIT).

Libraries
- sherpa-onnx (Apache License 2.0).
- PyMuPDF and MuPDF, which read PDF text (GNU Affero General Public License
  version 3, or a commercial licence from Artifex).
- Python and JavaScript dependencies listed in pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
  package.json, and package-lock.json, under their own licences.
- Inter and Piazzolla fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1), bundled with their
  licence files in src/stellis/static/fonts.
- vitallens 0.4.8 by Rouast Labs (MIT), vendored with its licence and face
  detection model in src/stellis/static/vendor/vitallens. Its browser build
  bundles TensorFlow.js (Apache License 2.0). Stellis Health runs only its
  local POS and CHROM methods, in the browser, and never calls the VitalLens
  API.

Test fixture
- tests/fixtures/jfk.wav is the speech sample distributed with whisper.cpp (MIT).

Condition lookup metadata
- src/stellis/condition_terms.json contains a title-based subset of English
  condition names, aliases and page URLs from the MedlinePlus.gov health-topic
  XML generated October 24, 2026, U.S. National Library of Medicine.
  https://medlineplus.gov/xml.html
  Rebuild with scripts/vendor_condition_terms.py and the source ZIP named in
  the JSON. Only metadata is retained; third-party linked articles are not bundled.
